Call of Duty modern warfare's DMZ mode  is a Sandbox style extraction Royale  mode with a steep learning curve let's  call it escape from tarkov light and  trust me there are plenty of things I  bet you didn't know you could do there's  also some really cool rewards to chase  so if you want to hop in I've got some  rapid fire tips on how to improve your  game  DMZ is a mode where you need to have a  goal in mind if you know what you're  after you'll make your life a lot easier  just wandering around the map means  you're gonna have a bad time because the  AI are super angry like seriously think  of DMZ at first as a place to complete  faction missions I'm talking resource  farming exploding vehicles or snacking  kills with certain weapons check those  objectives off your list and get out of  there and you're good if you're like me  extracting after having accomplished  something is the way to go also don't be  afraid to extract early if you stumbled  on any good gear like a three-played  vest especially if your teammates look a  little scrubby this way you don't die  and lose your hard-earned rewards now  that's not to say you can't make things  low stakes and just mess around just be  sure to leave your good guns behind so  you don't lose them  if you're without a squad in DMZ use  your ping wheel and select the option to  ask people to join you you can in theory  fill your squad back up and just keep  going also keep a faction Mission around  you can activate three at a time which  you can do solo if you do find yourself  without a squad  strength in numbers is real especially  in difficult situations your odds of  surviving are greater with a strong  Squad so keep everyone healthy and well  stocked ping good items for your squad  or be a bro and grab some things they  need if they've got a full load be sure  to hand out ammo like it's candy  now if you find yourself alone and  outgunned with high-level players all  around there is a lesser-known way to  extract simply hit up a hostage Rescue  Mission and if you succeed a chopper  comes in to pick up the hostage that you  can also get on pretty clutch if you're  too far from a normal extraction late in  the game if you're feeling ballsy and  want some more action you can scoop some  gas masks from the helicopter and just  bail and head back to the battlefield  if there is one thing you need to do at  the start of every round it's focused on  getting a two to three plate armor vest  the AI does not play around they hit  hard and you'll be chewing through armor  constantly if you don't randomly find  armor vest the best way to do this is to  gather local junk keep an eye on the  price of that junk and then sell it at a  buy station if you don't have enough go  buy a key card to a local stronghold  where you'll usually find better gear if  you have a tough time the cave complex  is a safe bed for good items in my  experience keep in mind that in general  items in the game follow a sort of logic  for example you're likely to find  medical items in bathrooms  once you get a grasp on Faction missions  it is time to go for bigger rewards  there are a few big ones but be aware  that many of these rewards will vastly  increase the chance of you winding up in  more battle royale style PvP with other  players the first you'll notice each  round is when other players grab a  weapons case and get marked on the map  although you can grab and extract with  the weapons case a total of seven times  in my opinion the first and the last  rewards are the best the first  extraction gets you the barrier tape rpk  blueprint which is a very good weapon  for this mode packing a high capacity  drum magazine and incendiary rounds Plus  I mean just look at this thing the  seventh time you extract with the case  though is nice because you get this  really cool chemist skin the other huge  PVP reward in the game right now is to  head to a radiation Zone find the  chemist and extract with their m13b only  one person in your party gets the weapon  however players are reporting that if  you load back into a round with your  squad and the person with it drops it  for you at an extraction you can get it  without fighting the chemist again  now if you get the weapon case other  teams will come after you so make sure  you bring along the Speedy ride or a  chopper and then get to the nearest  extraction Point fast I saw some squads  roam around the map trying to confuse  other players which extraction point  that we're gonna use but this just gave  the server more time to chase them down  now this will vary based on your  preference but if you don't have a good  Contraband gun or blueprint with you at  the start of a round I recommend going  for an rpk these lmgs are high capacity  and great for PVE because you'll have  plenty of situations where you don't  have time to reload mid battle and you  need a lot of bullets  [Music]  you can always take equipment with you  into the DMZ for free take the ammo box  just just do it you don't want to run  out of ammo right and I mean come on do  I need to say more about this  [Music]  now you have protected slots that unlock  as you complete faction missions these  let you take a weapon from your regular  inventory into DMZ but if you die they  go into a lengthy two hour cooldown  period extracting successfully lowers  that cooldown and also there's another  way scattered around the maps are  dumpsters find one and deposit cash to  lower your cooldown timer  [Music]  just like in Warzone if you catch a  straggler from an enemy Squad and you  knock them rather than finishing them  off you can interrogate them to find  where their buddies are super Nifty and  worth the extra effort knowledge is  power am I right  you [ __ ] where are they  there are times when vehicles are key to  your survival in DMZ and they run out of  gas you can repair and refuel them at  gas stations however if you're in a bad  spot already and the enemy Presence at  gas stations might make this a no-go  fortunately a lot of gas stations have  gas cans that you can grab as long as  you're a passenger in a moving vehicle  you can go into your backpack and select  the gas can then refuel your vehicle at  any time  don't forget you can have another gun in  your medium or large backpack like if  you want a sniper rifle handy for later  on in matches you also get to keep these  as Contraband when you extract that  means if you're low on Contraband  weapons feel free to go in grab three  weapons and bail if you find the  Basilisk revolver at a police station  for example pack it for a later faction  mission where you need it for headshots  you can also just use your own basilisk  blueprint to complete that faction  Mission as a matter of fact while we're  on the subject DMZ is one of the best  ways to level guns in Modern Warfare 2.  extracting with a gun in DMZ will unlock  its base model across the entire game  if your squad gets overwhelmed and  downed by AI near a body of water be a  pal and crawl into deep water before  dying your squad can dive down and  revive you which is a much safer way to  do it than in the open side note you can  find loot underwater sometimes and I  mean if we're on the topic of saving  your squad the revive pistol is very  powerful it can not only revive at a  distance but comes with self-revive  a lot of missions and activities like  drilling safes and DMZ will call in  waves of enemies on Choppers and in  vehicles you do not need to sit around  waiting for them to attack you it can be  easier to shoot down the helicopters or  blow up Vehicles before the bad guys  ever get a chance to exit alternatively  if you think other players are around  you might want to leave baddies alive at  objectives or extraction points to slow  them down and give you a better Fighting  Chance the Armored Cars enemies show up  in are pretty good and you can steal  them  [Music]  so you asked me how to tell other  players apart well the short answer is  there isn't an easy answer once you play  a bunch of rounds of DMZ you start to  get a feel for what types of missions  other players show up at more often in  some matches you don't see any other  players and in some rounds you find  other squads at the very first  stronghold that you hit up if you hear a  lot of gunfire it's usually other  players taking on the AI the best thing  you can do is occasionally pause and  listen other players will also just move  differently like closing doors and  dolphin diving even though they  physically look different from the  enemies it can be hard to make out at a  distance other tails are if you pay  attention to the map the game will tell  you what objectives are being attacked  and if it's near you keep an eye on  Modern Warfare 2 has a ton of great  custom settings and although these  suggestions are not Universal here's  what you should consider doing swap  armor plate Behavior to apply all so it  only takes one long button press to load  all your armor plates if you are on  controller except plunging underwater to  plunge freely so you can escape quickly  underwater just by aiming down and set  parachute Auto deploy to off so you can  pull your shoot closer to the ground and  avoid getting shot out of the air swap  to automatic Sprint and also tactical  Sprint Behavior to single tap Sprint so  you walk or run based on how far you  hold the stick or the button down and  you only need to click once to tax frame  this lets you get to cover way more  quickly try interact reload Behavior  with prioritize reload so you can more  quickly loot items with a button press  but won't accidentally pick up items in  a gunfighter when you meant to reload  set controller button layout to Tactical  which will let you crouch while shooting  without taking your fingers off the  aiming stick  now stealth is very difficult in DMZ but  not impossible According to some Reddit  users if you pack a long range sniper  rifle with a suppressor and you don't  miss you can drop quite a few enemies  before the alert do make sure your aim  is true though the AI seems to have some  brains and can pinpoint you pretty fast  if alerted you can definitely pick up  stragglers using executions but it's  unclear if you need to pack a melee  Focus attack to stay quiet try using a  throwing knife also and remember in  stealth silence is deadly  it's important to remember you are not  safe when extracting and players can  jump on board at any time even as you  take off as mentioned before it's  honestly good to leave a few AI enemies  around the extract as an early warning  system alternatively players have  discovered you can jump on or hang off  the side of the helicopter to get out  with a slightly less chance of being  spotted by an enemy team already on  board  DMZ is shaping up to be a mode with a  lot of secrets so let us know what you  found that you wish you knew before  starting thanks for watching  foreign  [Music]
 

